   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ECO111 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.6</span>\n<h2>Student tasks & constructive questions</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">The rules you are held to (attendance, preparation, exam eligibility) — verbatim.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 13497 · Decision 1318/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 27/11/2025 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ECO111 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.6</span>\n<h2>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên & câu hỏi kiến tạo</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Những quy định bạn phải tuân theo (chuyên cần, chuẩn bị bài, điều kiện dự thi) — nguyên văn.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 13497 · QĐ 1318/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 27/11/2025 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student tasks (verbatim)</h3>\n<p>+ Class attendance is strongly encouraged. Attend at least 80% of class hours in order to be accepted to the final examination<br><br>+ Read textbooks and other materials in advance before class<br><br>+ Actively participate in class activities<br><br>+ Complete all homework assignments and other tasks given by the instructor<br><br>+ Use personal laptop in class only for learning purposes<br><br>+ Don’t have private conversations or arrive at class late, which can disrupt the learning environment of the class</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<p>+ Class attendance is strongly encouraged. Attend at least 80% of class hours in order to be accepted to the final examination<br><br>+ Read textbooks and other materials in advance before class<br><br>+ Actively participate in class activities<br><br>+ Complete all homework assignments and other tasks given by the instructor<br><br>+ Use personal laptop in class only for learning purposes<br><br>+ Don’t have private conversations or arrive at class late, which can disrupt the learning environment of the class</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions (26)</h3>\n<p>Questions the syllabus asks you to think through before or during the session — try answering them yourself first.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo (26)</h3>\n<p>Câu hỏi syllabus yêu cầu bạn suy nghĩ trước/trong buổi học — tự trả lời trước khi xem bài.</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Session<br><small>Buổi</small></th><th>Code<br><small>Mã</small></th><th>Question (verbatim)<br><small>Câu hỏi (nguyên văn)</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td>ĐN3.1</td><td>1. Money runs the world! And the money just exists where there is a buyer, seller and exchange of goods, which is called “the market”. What is the market and why is it so important for people?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td>ĐN3.2</td><td>2. The market has two components: demand and supply. How was the demand created and how does it change?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td>ĐN3.3</td><td>3. The market has two components: demand and supply. How was the supply created and how does it change?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td>ĐN3.4</td><td>4. How was the price and the quantity of goods or services in a market set up?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>9</td><td>ĐN3.5</td><td>5. How can we predict the price and quantity of goods to get more benefit?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>10</td><td>ĐN4.1</td><td>Imagine that you now controlled a company/a farm. You must increase the revenue of your company to have a better performance. Using the concept “Elasticity” to find the answer of this below question: 1. Should you increase the price of goods to have more revenue?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>11</td><td>ĐN4.2</td><td>2. Should you produce more quantity to increase the revenue?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>12</td><td>ĐN4.3</td><td>3. How can you get more revenue by the understanding of Elasticity?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>13</td><td>ĐN5.1</td><td>Imagine that now you are the president of our nation. You must make good policies for the people’s living. Give your opinions with this problems:</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>13</td><td>ĐN5.2</td><td>1. If the price of necessary things (rice, pork, face marks,..) is too high, should the government set up the limitation of price (maximum price) to help the poor buyer?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>14</td><td>ĐN5.2</td><td>2. If the price of necessary things (rice, pork,….) is too low, should the government set up the limitation of price (minimum price) to protect the producers/farmers?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>14</td><td>ĐN5.4</td><td>3. How does the market change if the government imposes taxes on buyers?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>15</td><td>ĐN5.5</td><td>4. How does Elasticity change Taxes Incidence?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>16</td><td>ĐN6.1</td><td>1. How is the Consumer Surplus measured?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>17</td><td>ĐN6.2</td><td>2. How is the Producer Surplus measured?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>18</td><td>ĐN6.3</td><td>3. How is Market Efficiency (Total Surplus) measured?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>18</td><td>ĐN6.4</td><td>4. Why are Markets usually a good way to organize economic activity?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>25</td><td>ĐN9.1</td><td>In economics, we assume that a firm only wants to have maximum Profit, that equals Revenue minus Cost.The Revenue is so simple to calculate, equal The Price times The Quantity of Goods. But, The Cost is more complex, and hard to calculate. We must try to answer:<br>1. How many kinds of Cost in a firm’s production?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>26</td><td>ĐN9.2</td><td>2. How can we reduce the cost, so we can have cheaper products in a market?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>27</td><td>ĐN9.3</td><td>3. Why does Cost directly affect Profit of a company?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>34</td><td>ĐN12.1</td><td>1. What happens if a market (medicine, electricity, water…) has only one seller?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>35</td><td>ĐN12.2</td><td>2. How about the price, quantity, efficiency of a market (medicine, electricity, water…) has only one seller?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>36</td><td>ĐN12.3</td><td>3. How can a government control the only one-seller market?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>37</td><td>ĐN13.1</td><td>1. What happens when a market has many sellers, many buyers, and the products are not identical (books, clothes,…)?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>38</td><td>ĐN13.2</td><td>2. How about the price, quantity, efficiency?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>39</td><td>ĐN13.3</td><td>3. How can the government manage this kind of market?</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13497\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13497</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13497\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13497</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
